@page "/sortable/simple"

<PageTitle>Sortable - Simple · Bdnd</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Sortable - Simple</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">
        React DnD's sortable recipe. Each card is <em>both</em> a <code>BdndDraggable</code> and a
        <code>BdndDropTarget</code>. While dragging, the <code>OnHover</code> handler measures the hovered card
        (<code>BdndInterop.GetBoundingClientRectAsync</code>), compares the pointer
        (<code>Monitor.GetClientOffset()</code>) against its midpoint and reorders the list live. Reordering happens
        during hover, not on drop. The keyboard reorders the same way - <kbd>Space</kbd> on a card, then each arrow
        key moves it one place - because a keyboard drag runs <code>OnHover</code> as it moves too. The list itself is
        a drop target as well, so the gaps between the cards are no "no-drop" zones. For most lists the
        <a href="sortable/indicators">drop indicators</a> page shows a simpler way, which measures nothing.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-demo">
    <BdndProvider>
        @* the list accepts cards too, so the gaps between cards are not "no-drop" zones *@
        <BdndDropTarget TItem="SortableCard.DragItem" Accept="@ItemTypes.Card" style="max-width:24rem;">
            @foreach (var (card, index) in _cards.Select((c, i) => (c, i)))
            {
                <SortableCard Card="card" Index="index" OnMove="Move" @key="card.Id" />
            }
        </BdndDropTarget>
    </BdndProvider>

    <p class="demo-caption sortable-order">Order: @string.Join(", ", _cards.Select(c => c.Text))</p>
</div>

<DemoCode />

@code {
    private readonly List<SortableCard.CardModel> _cards =
    [
        new(1, "Write the docs"),
        new(2, "Review the PR"),
        new(3, "Ship the release"),
        new(4, "Celebrate"),
        new(5, "Sleep"),
    ];

    private void Move((int From, int To) move)
    {
        var (from, to) = move;
        if (from < 0 || from >= _cards.Count || to < 0 || to >= _cards.Count) return;
        var card = _cards[from];
        _cards.RemoveAt(from);
        _cards.Insert(to, card);
    }
}
